<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="/log" id="log">

    <tldr>
        <p>
            <format style="italic">Log a carry inside a carry ticket.</format>
        </p>

        <p><br/></p>

        <p>
            <format style="bold">Allowed in DMs:</format>
            :x: No
        </p>

        <p>
            <format style="bold">Default permission required:</format>
            <code>None</code>
        </p>
    </tldr>

    <chapter title="Description" id="description">
        <p>
            Use this command within a carry ticket channel to log completed carries. The bot validates the ticket,
            prompts for confirmation, and records the log, awarding you score based on the carry tier and difficulty.
        </p>
        <p>
            This command is only available in ticket channels that have a <code>relatedCarryTier</code> configured.
            The ticket panel must be linked to a carry tier for the log command to function. See
            <a href="Ticket-Panel-Configuration.md"/> for details on setting up carry integration.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Arguments" id="arguments" collapsible="true">
        <table style="header-row">
            <tr>
                <td>Name</td>
                <td>Type</td>
                <td>Description</td>
                <td>Optional?</td>
                <td>Additional</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>amount</code></td>
                <td>Integer</td>
                <td>Number of carries to log.</td>
                <td>:x: No</td>
                <td>Min: 1, Max: 200</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>carry-difficulty</code></td>
                <td>Autocompleted String</td>
                <td>Difficulty identifier of the carry.</td>
                <td>:x: No</td>
                <td> </td>
            </tr>
        </table>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Examples" id="examples" collapsible="true">
        <chapter title="Log a carry" id="ex-log">
            <code-block lang="bash">/log amount: 3 carry-difficulty: S</code-block>
            <img alt="log-confirm.png" src="log-confirm.png" width="325" style="inline" border-effect="rounded"/>
        </chapter>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Notes" id="notes" collapsible="true">
        <list>
            <li>
                The ticket channel must be associated with a ticket panel that has a <code>relatedCarryTier</code> configured.
            </li>
            <li>
                The carry difficulty must match one of the difficulties configured for the related carry tier.
            </li>
            <li>
                After logging, your score is updated and can be viewed with <a href="score.topic">/score</a>.
            </li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="See Also" id="see-also">
        <list>
            <li><a href="Ticket-System.md">Ticket System</a>: overview of how carry tickets work</li>
            <li><a href="Ticket-Panel-Configuration.md"/>: configure <code>relatedCarryTier</code> and <code>relatedCarryDifficulty</code></li>
            <li><a href="score.topic"/>: your score increases from successful logs</li>
            <li><a href="leaderboard.topic"/>: see how logs affect rankings</li>
            <li><a href="manage-score.topic"/>: admins can resolve edge cases manually</li>
            <li><a href="Carry-Difficulty.md"/>: the Carry Difficulty you enter</li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

</topic>
